					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Mixing and Mastering</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Infi-Note</b> on <b>September 01, 2007, 05:36:12 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: martyfever on September 01, 2007, 01:08:42 am</div><div class="quote">Hi Infi-Note, you can get hold of me at Jupiter studio- 206 6331363, it&#039;s in Wallingford. If that&#039;s hard for you to drop by then you could send it to my P.O. box- 99443, Seattle, WA, 98139-0443. I&#039;d like a data CDR of the mix, make sure the mix is not clipped/maxed out and I&#039;d prefer it to have no DSP/limiting done to it, make sure to note on it the file type/sample rate and bit depth.<br />looking forward to it,<br />Martin<br /></div><br /><br />Thanks a lot, I&#039;ll be sure to send you something.&nbsp; I usually save all my mixes once before i do any limiting to it anyways so it wont be a problem.</div>
