					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: coo-blah-kai on August 15, 2007, 11:25:18 pm</div><div class="quote"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: martyfever on August 13, 2007, 09:19:14 pm</div><div class="quote">I do record, mix and Master. I don&#039;t normally charge by the song but by the hour or day. Label rates are quite high but I charge a lower rate for indie/self financed projects - $65 per hour or $600 for a 10 hour day. <br /></div><br />*Opens wallet and dust puffs from the seams.* slowly walks away...... <br /></div><br /><br />Dude really isn&#039;t charging that much for a 1/2 million dollar studio <i>(I currently work in a studio in SF that charges  $400/hr)</i>...you gotta think of it as investing in your career, because even if you&#039;re the best rapper in town, if your engineer doesn&#039;t know what he&#039;s doing you might as well be printing your name on frisbees.<br /><br />But, for all you broke cats, hit up my studio in Seattle, the Boiler Room...we&#039;re running a deal for the month of September <i>(in celebration of Grayskul&#039;s 9/11 Rhymesayers/Warner release Bloody Radio)</i> where you can get <b>5 hours for $100.</b> Every artist who has ever recorded at the Boiler Room has gotten airplay from their sessions, and many of them are now signed.<br /><br />www.seattleboilerroom.com<br />www.myspace.com/seattleboilerroom<br /><br /><b>Support Grayskul</b> and show the industry that Seattle&#039;s hot, and <i>maybe you&#039;ll be the next cat signing a deal!</i><br />WWW.MYSPACE.COM/GRAYSKUL<br /><br /><br /><br /><br /><br /></div>
